# Intro
A single, fixed-mass star at the center of a uniform, periodic glass-IC gas
box, with photoelectric heating on (LW/FUV injection, no Yukawa propagation)
and real Grackle cooling. Checks the basic sign and rough magnitude of
Grackle's photoelectric-heating response to the injected LW/FUV field: gas
near the star should reach a HIGHER equilibrium temperature with
`GEARFeedback:with_photoelectric_heating: 1` than with it set to `0`,
otherwise identical configuration. This is a coarse direction/magnitude
sanity check, not a quantitative PDR-physics comparison (see
`isrf_photoelectric_heating_check.py`).

## Propagation
`LW_FUV_propagation: 0`: this example is about the thermal response to
whatever field a particle receives directly from the star, not about
propagation numerics (see the sibling `ISRFHyperbolicPropagation` for
that). Only gas within the star's own SPH kernel is illuminated.

## Cooling
Unlike `ISRFHyperbolicPropagation`,
`GrackleCooling:disable_cooling_for_debugging` is `0`: this example's whole
point is to measure the gas's actual thermal response, so cooling and
heating are both fully active.

## Metallicity
Solar (`Z/Zsun=1`, `run.sh`'s `initial_metallicity`): the receiver-side dust
extinction this example also exercises needs a nonzero, known metallicity.

# Configure
```
./configure --with-chemistry=GEAR_10 --with-feedback=GEAR --with-cooling=grackle_0 --with-stars=GEAR --with-sink=GEAR --with-star-formation=GEAR --with-tracers=GEAR --with-kernel=wendland-C2 --with-grackle=path/to/grackle
make -j
```
`--with-tracers=GEAR` is required: the tracers module registers the
`FUVSpecificEnergies`/`LWSpecificEnergies` snapshot output (the fields
themselves live on `struct part`'s `feedback_data`). Photoelectric heating
itself only needs `GrackleCooling:with_metal_cooling: 1` (set in
`params.yml`); any Grackle cooling mode works, `grackle_0` included.

# Run
Two runs are needed, identical except for `with_photoelectric_heating`:
```
with_pe_heating=1 run_name=heating_on  ./run.sh
with_pe_heating=0 run_name=heating_off ./run.sh
```
Override any other parameter via the matching env var -- gas density
(`gas_density`, atom/cm^3), gas particle mass (`gas_mass`, Msun), star mass
and type (`star_mass`, `star_type`), resolution level (`level`, N =
`(2**level)**3` gas particles), run duration and stepping (`time_end`,
`dt_max`, `delta_time`), metallicity (`initial_metallicity`), and thread
count (`n_threads`); see `run.sh` for the full list and defaults.
`run_name=<dir> ./run.sh` moves the run's outputs into `<dir>` once done, to
keep the two runs' outputs side by side.

# Checking
```
python3 isrf_photoelectric_heating_check.py \
    --on-snapshot  "heating_on/snap/snapshot_*.hdf5" \
    --off-snapshot "heating_off/snap/snapshot_*.hdf5"
```
Bins gas by radius from the star at each run's final snapshot, restricts
the comparison to bins where the on-run's own LW/FUV field is
non-negligible, and checks there that (1) the heating-on temperature is
higher than the heating-off temperature and (2) it stays below a
physically-motivated ceiling (1e6 K) rather than showing signs of a
numerical blow-up. Produces a comparison plot (`--output`, default
`isrf_photoelectric_heating_check.png`).
